  <prompt>In SprkChatAgentFactory.BuildWorkspaceStateBlock, trim the workspace-state block so it carries ONLY {type,label,active} per tab (no ambient widget content), and thread the client-supplied active-item handle {id,type,label} into the prompt's single active-item slot.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. .NET 8 Minimal API + AI agent-factory expertise; comfortable reasoning about the ADR-015 id-not-content boundary and threading a bounded handle through existing seams without forking Services/Ai internals.</role>
  <goal>The workspace-state block emits {type,label,active} per tab plus exactly one {id,type,label} active-item handle — and no item content anywhere in the block.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-03 + FR-04 (server). The workspace-state block is built in `BuildWorkspaceStateBlock` (~:1469). FR-03 trims it to ONLY {type,label,active} per tab — no ambient widget content of any kind. FR-04 (server half) threads the active-item handle {id,type,label} — published client-side by the task-001 conduit and carried on the chat request — into a single active-item slot in the prompt. This is the id-not-content boundary (ADR-015 Path A, honest): the label is a thin identity slice; all real content is tool-fetched by id downstream (Phase 2 parity tools). The handle shape is exactly {id,type,label} — if honoring it would need more than that, STOP (see escalation). Runs after 010 (same file). Consume `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams; do NOT fork `Services/Ai/` internals (redesign-r2 sole owner). A characterization/snapshot test must prove the block has no item-content fields.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/SprkChatAgentFactory.cs (BuildWorkspaceStateBlock ~:1469)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs (chat request DTO carrying the active-item handle — reuse the R2 activeContext threading pattern)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">The prompt carries {type,label,active} per tab + one {id,type,label} handle — NO item content ever enters the prompt. All content is tool-fetched by id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">No classifier, no second dispatch surface — deterministic prompt assembly only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Consume Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ seams; do NOT fork Services/Ai/ internals (redesign-r2 sole owner); no AI-internal types into CRUD code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF §10: publish size ≤60 MB compressed (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs) — measure and report the delta.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope clause: trim the block + thread the {id,type,label} handle only. Do NOT add layout-tab visibility (010) or build any parity tool (Phase 2).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r3/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r3/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read BuildWorkspaceStateBlock and inventory every field it currently emits per tab.</step>
    <step order="2">Trim the per-tab emission to exactly {type,label,active} — remove all ambient widget content.</step>
    <step order="3">Thread the client-supplied active-item handle {id,type,label} (reuse the R2 activeContext request threading) into a single active-item slot in the block.</step>
    <step order="4">Add a characterization/snapshot test asserting the block has no item-content fields (only type/label/active per tab + one handle).</step>
    <step order="5">Add a test for the single active-item slot (exactly one handle; empty when none published).</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build + dotnet publish size check; record absolute + delta.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If honoring the active-item handle requires more than {id,type,label} (e.g. any content field to make it usable), STOP and escalate (ADR-015) rather than widening the handle. If PublicContracts/ lacks a seam for the handle threading, coordinate with spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2 rather than forking Services/Ai/.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>BuildWorkspaceStateBlock emits richer per-tab state today (R2 ambient content); no single active-item handle slot exists.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — trim the existing emission + add one handle slot fed by the request; no new method or store.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The prompt keeps ambient content (ADR-015 drift + token bloat) and the Assistant has no id to key per-item actions to — the §5.5 handle-driven flow can't run.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/SprkChatAgentFactory.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs (if the handle needs request threading)</output>
    <output type="test">BuildWorkspaceStateBlock characterization/snapshot test</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A snapshot/characterization test of BuildWorkspaceStateBlock output shows no item-content fields — only {type,label,active} per tab.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The block carries exactly one {id,type,label} active-item handle when the client publishes one.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">When no active item is published, the active-item slot is empty (no stale/duplicate handle).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The handle carries only id/type/label — no content field (negative case: any content field fails the governance test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>NFR-04 governance — this is the id-not-content boundary the project rests on. Serialize after 010 (same file). Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR; coordinate redesign-r2 seams.

COMPLETED 2026-08-10 (opus/xhigh, FULL). THREE changes (the first is the owner-approved re-point beyond the original POML):
(A) RE-POINT: `BuildWorkspaceStateBlock` is now fed from the LIVE tabs (`session.Tabs` / `StoredSession.Tabs`, written by the client via PATCH /sessions/{id}/tabs → `SaveTabsAsync`) instead of the runtime-inert `IWorkspaceStateService.GetTabsAsync` (write path retired by AIR2-075). The ChatEndpoints SendMessage handler loads the stored session via `ISessionPersistenceService.LoadSessionAsync` and maps `StoredWorkspaceTab{id,widgetType,widgetData,displayName}` → `WorkspaceTab` (new private `MapStoredTabsToWorkspaceTabs`), passed to `CreateAgentAsync` as a new `liveTabs` param. `CreateAgentAsync` UNIONs `liveTabs` with pinned durable rows from `IWorkspaceStateService` (live rows win on same id). visibleToAssistant reconciliation: `StoredWorkspaceTab` has NO `visibleToAssistant` field → live tabs default visible=true (they appear — the point). Persisting the FR-01/FR-02 toggle through the live path needs a client PATCH-DTO field → FLAGGED as follow-up, NOT done (no client change).
(B) TRIM (FR-03): per-tab emission is now EXACTLY `- Tab {n}{(active)}: widgetType={type} label="{label}"` — all ambient widget content removed (FormatVisibleStateFields no longer wired into the block; retained + noted). label = DisplayName ?? derived identity name (dashboardName/filename/subject) ?? widgetType.
(C) HANDLE (FR-04): added `ChatActiveItem{id,type,label}` on `ChatSendMessageRequest` + `WorkspaceActiveItemHandle` (Models/Workspace, 3-field record) threaded into a single `### Active Item` slot (id/type/label only; empty when none).
Task 010's layout-tab identity variant PRESERVED (composes — the derivation special-cases still run; only the emission format changed).
Tests: `SprkChatAgentFactoryWorkspaceStateTests` rewritten to the trimmed contract + governance/handle tests (38 pass); `Pillar9PrivacyFilterTests` updated (3 pass). Full BFF unit suite 10252 passed / 0 failed / 101 skipped. Build 0 errors. Publish 48.44 MB compressed incl PDBs (baseline ~49.63 → −1.19 MB; ≤60 MB ceiling OK).</notes>
